/// Chapter 5 of the guide, written from md-docs/05-state-and-reactivity.md by
/// scripts/site-from-guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page StateAndReactivity(path: "/docs/guide/state", title: "State and reactivity", description: "state, derived, effect, actions and let, persist, timers, element handles and the browser's values.", layout: DocsShell("State and reactivity", chapter: "Chapter 5", blurb: "Reactivity here is fine-grained: a state is a signal, and only the thing that read it updates.", sections: [Anchor(id: "state", label: "state"), Anchor(id: "derived", label: "derived"), Anchor(id: "effect", label: "effect"), Anchor(id: "actions-and-locals", label: "Actions and locals"), Anchor(id: "persist", label: "persist"), Anchor(id: "timers", label: "Timers"), Anchor(id: "ownership-what-leaves-leaves", label: "Ownership: what leaves, leaves"), Anchor(id: "element-handles", label: "Element handles"), Anchor(id: "the-browser-as-values", label: "The browser as values"), Anchor(id: "where-values-come-from-in-order", label: "Where values come from, in order")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/elements", prevLabel: "4. Elements", nextTo: "/docs/guide/events-and-forms", nextLabel: "6. Events and forms")) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("WebFluent's reactivity is fine-grained: a `state` is a signal, and anything that reads it — a text, an attribute, a `derived` value, an `effect`, a style splice — follows it. There is no re-render of a tree; the thing that read the value is what updates.")

        Heading("state", id: "state").h2

        CodeBlock("page Counter(path: \"/\") \{\n    state count = 0                  // inferred: Number\n    state name: String = \"\"          // declared\n    state items: [String] = []       // a list of strings\n    state selected: String? = null   // may be null\n    state user = \{ name: \"Sam\", tags: [\"a\"] \}   // a map literal: its fields are its type\n\n    Text(\"\{name\} has clicked \{count\} times\")\n    Button(\"+\") \{ on click \{ count = count + 1 \} \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("A `state` is declared at the top of a page, component or store body, with an initial value. Its type is read off the value, or written after a colon; [chapter 10](/docs/guide/types) has the type language. Assigning a value of another type is an error (`T01`).\n\nState is written only in an imperative block — a handler, an action, an effect: `count = count + 1`, `user.name = \"Ann\"`, `items[0] = \"x\"`, or through a method that changes it in place (`items.push(\"x\")`). The static paint seeds every state with its initial value, so a pre-rendered page shows what the first paint would.")

        Heading("derived", id: "derived").h2

        Markdown("A derived value is computed from state and recomputed when any state it read changes:")

        CodeBlock("page Cart(path: \"/\") \{\n    state items = [\{ name: \"Pen\", price: 2.5, qty: 4 \}, \{ name: \"Pad\", price: 6, qty: 1 \}]\n    state taxRate = 0.2\n    derived subtotal = items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.price * i.qty, 0)\n    derived total = subtotal * (1 + taxRate)\n    derived empty = items.length == 0\n\n    Text(\"Subtotal: \{format(subtotal, .currency)\}\")\n    Text(\"Total: \{format(total, .currency)\}\")\n    if empty \{ Text(\"Your cart is empty.\").muted \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("A derived value may read other derived values and call actions. It is never assigned to. It is seeded in the static paint from the initial state.")

        Heading("effect", id: "effect").h2

        Markdown("An effect runs once, and again whenever a state it read changes. Its `cleanup \{ \}` block runs before the next run and when the page (or the branch the effect lives in) leaves:")

        CodeBlock("page Watch(path: \"/\") \{\n    state query = \"\"\n    state hits = 0\n    effect \{\n        log(\"query is now \{query\}\")\n        hits = hits + 1\n    \}\n    effect \{\n        document.title = \"Search: \{query\}\"\n        cleanup \{ document.title = \"Search\" \}\n    \}\n    Input(bind: query, placeholder: \"Search\")\n    Text(\"\{hits\} runs\")\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("Use effects for the world outside the page — the document title, a third-party widget, a subscription. Keep computation in `derived`.")

        Heading("Actions and locals", id: "actions-and-locals").h2

        Markdown("An action is a named function of the page, component or store. Its body is an imperative block: assignments, `let` locals, calls, `if`, `for`, `try`, `return`, `await`.")

        CodeBlock("page Todos(path: \"/\") \{\n    state items: [String] = []\n    state draft = \"\"\n\n    action add() \{\n        let text = draft.trim()\n        if text == \"\" \{ return \}\n        items.push(text)\n        draft = \"\"\n    \}\n\n    action remove(index: Number) \{\n        items = items.filter((_, i) => i != index)\n    \}\n\n    action load() \{\n        let r = await fetch(\"/api/todos\")\n        let \{ todos \} = r\n        items = todos\n    \}\n\n    Input(bind: draft, placeholder: \"What needs doing?\") \{ on keydown(e) \{ if e.key == \"Enter\" \{ add() \} \} \}\n    Button(\"Add\").primary \{ on click \{ add() \} \}\n    for item, i in items \{\n        Row \{ Text(item)  IconButton(icon: \"trash\", label: \"Remove\") \{ on click \{ remove(i) \} \} \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `let x = …` declares a local of the action (or handler). `let \{ a, b \} = m` and `let [x, y] = l` destructure.\n- `await` inside an action makes it asynchronous; `name.pending` is `true` while a call of it runs ([chapter 6](/docs/guide/events-and-forms#pending-actions)).\n- `for item in list \{ \}`, `for item, i in list \{ \}` and `for n in 1..=10 \{ \}` loop; `try \{ \} catch e \{ \}` guards a call that may fail; `return x` leaves with a value.\n- A page's action is called by name, `add()`; a store's through the store, `Todos.add()`.")

        Heading("persist", id: "persist").h2

        Markdown("`persist` is a `state` kept in the browser's storage across visits. It is read back on the next visit and written on every change:")

        CodeBlock("page Prefs(path: \"/\") \{\n    persist theme = \"light\"\n    persist perPage = 20\n    Select(bind: theme, label: \"Theme\") \{\n        Select.Option(\"Light\", value: \"light\")\n        Select.Option(\"Dark\", value: \"dark\")\n    \}\n    Slider(bind: perPage, min: 10, max: 100, step: 10, label: \"Rows per page\")\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("It works in a store too, where every page shares it. The key is the owner's name and the state's (`Prefs.theme`), so a page and a store may each have a `theme`. Storage that is blocked or full falls back to the initial value.")

        Heading("Timers", id: "timers").h2

        Markdown("`every(ms) \{ \}` repeats; `after(ms) \{ \}` fires once. Both stop when what declared them leaves the page — a branch that closes, a list item that is removed, a route that changes:")

        CodeBlock("page Clock(path: \"/\") \{\n    state seconds = 0\n    state toast: String? = \"Welcome\"\n    every(1000) \{ seconds = seconds + 1 \}\n    after(3000) \{ toast = null \}\n    Text(\"\{seconds\}s on this page\")\n    if let t = toast \{ Alert(t).info \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Heading("Ownership: what leaves, leaves", id: "ownership-what-leaves-leaves").h2

        Markdown("Everything a body creates — effects, timers, listeners, handles — belongs to the scope it was created in. When that scope's nodes leave (an `if` branch turns false, an item drops out of a `for`, a `match` arm changes, a route changes), the runtime disposes of them: intervals are cleared, effects fall silent, cleanups run. You never unsubscribe by hand.")

        Heading("Element handles", id: "element-handles").h2

        Markdown("`ref: name` on an element gives you a handle, read as the element itself:")

        CodeBlock("page Search(path: \"/\") \{\n    state q = \"\"\n    Input(bind: q, ref: box, placeholder: \"Search\")\n    Button(\"Focus the box\") \{ on click \{ box.focus() \} \}\n    Button(\"Clear\") \{ on click \{ q = \"\"  box.focus() \} \}\n    on key(\"/\") \{ box.focus() \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("The name is declared by its use; `box.value`, `box.scrollIntoView()`, anything the element has.")

        Heading("The browser as values", id: "the-browser-as-values").h2

        Markdown("Four names are always in scope, kept current by the runtime:")

        CodeBlock("page Where(path: \"/\") \{\n    Text(if viewport.md \{ \"wide\" \} else \{ \"narrow\" \})   // viewport.width, .height, .sm .md .lg .xl\n    derived tab = query.tab ?? \"all\"                      // the URL's ?tab=x\n    Text(\"Tab: \{tab\}\")\n    Text(\"Section: \{hash\}\")                               // the URL's #fragment\n    Text(\"Theme: \{theme\}\")                                // light, dark or system\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("Breakpoints: `sm` 640px, `md` 768px, `lg` 1024px, `xl` 1280px. A `state` you declare with one of these names shadows it. In the static paint they are unknown, so a condition on them renders as its live branch once hydrated.")

        Heading("Where values come from, in order", id: "where-values-come-from-in-order").h2

        Markdown("1. Route parameters and props (`slug`, `_ label`).\n2. `state`, `persist`, `derived`, `resource`, actions of the body.\n3. A `use`d store's members, through the store's name (`Cart.total`).\n4. Loop variables and arm bindings inside their block.\n5. Constants and `data` files, `env.X`, the browser's values.\n6. Browser globals: `window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `JSON`, `Math`, `Date`, `fetch`, `setTimeout`, `console`, `navigator`, `location`.")
    }
}
